 "recommendation": {
  "route": "graph route B1: prove the codimension-m GRAPH area formula first, then localize",
  "why": [
   "a graph map is injective by construction, so no InjOn hypothesis and no multiplicity",
   "its parameter projection is an EXPLICIT left inverse, which is exactly what obligation A3 lacks",
   "the volume factor sqrt(det(1 + adjoint A comp A)) was proved in the previous round and already agrees with the repository codimension-one graphJacobian",
   "obligation A4 does not arise at all, because a graph map differential is always injective"
  ],
  "cost_anchor": "the repository proved the codimension-one graph case in Analysis/AreaFormula.lean at 957 lines, alongside Analysis/ImplicitGraph.lean at 859 lines",
  "suggested_order": [
   "A1 continuity and measurability of normDet (low risk)",
   "B1 codimension-m graph area formula (2-3 rounds)",
   "A5 and A2 patching",
   "only then the codimension-m regular case of the coarea formula"
  ]
